  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nThere are meaningful model differences in the southern extent of\nstronger high pressure on Sunday over the southwest states into \nnorthern Mexico and the resulting differences in the amount of \nmoisture that may spread into portions of southern California. \nThose model solutions that maintain stronger high pressure farther\ninto northern Mexico have less moisture transport into southern \nCalifornia while those that are weaker with high pressure across \nnorthern Mexico allow for a greater transport of moisture and \nclouds into portions of southern California on Sunday. \n\nThe current forecast shows less cooling of high temperatures and\nless increase in clouds and chances for afternoon thunderstorms\nover the mountains for Sunday with continued slow cooling into\nMonday. Beyond the moisture surge and resulting cooling of high\ntemperatures that could occur on Sunday, gradual cooling and\ndrying will continue into the middle of next week, but with high \ntemperatures still around 5 degrees above average for inland \nareas. High temperatures for next Wednesday would range from the \nmid 70s to around 80 near the coast to the 90s to 102 for the \nInland Empire with 108 to 112 for the lower deserts.\n\nHigh pressure for the end of next week could be even stronger than\nfor the end of this week.",
